From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: preserve Trek Tech menu trails on detail entry

Trek Tech constructs its orange topic menu with a single trails-enabled
sprite, stamping each row permanently onto the stage.  Its PathZone text
sprite is initially authored over that area and later moved to the breadcrumb
below the menu.  ScummVM clears the sprite's complete old bounding box during
that move, erasing the stamped rows; no live sprite remains to redraw them.

The menu has already painted over the old PathZone before the relocation.
Suppress that obsolete cleanup only for Trek Tech's known PathZone move,
leaving every other sprite and game on the normal redraw path.
---
 engines/director/window.cpp | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/engines/director/window.cpp b/engines/director/window.cpp
--- a/engines/director/window.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/window.cpp
@@ -327,7 +327,19 @@ bool Window::render(bool forceRedraw, Graphics::ManagedSurface *blitTo) {
 
 		debugC(7, kDebugImages, "Window::render(): drawing channel %d", (int)i);
 
-		if (!chan->_lastTrail) {
+		// Trek Tech builds the orange topic menu by moving one trails-enabled
+		// sprite down the right side and stamping each row onto the stage.  Its
+		// PathZone text sprite is authored over that same area, then moved to the
+		// breadcrumb below the menu once the detail view is ready.  Clearing the
+		// PathZone's old bounding box at that point erases the already-stamped
+		// menu rows; there are no live sprites from which to redraw those pixels.
+		// The menu has already painted over the old PathZone, so retain that
+		// rectangle only for this one authored-to-breadcrumb relocation.
+		bool preserveTrekPathZoneTrails = strcmp(g_director->getGameId(), "trektech") == 0 &&
+				i == 19 && chan->_sprite && chan->_sprite->_castId.member == 151 &&
+				chan->_lastRenderedBbox.top < 150 && bbox.top > 200;
+
+		if (!chan->_lastTrail && !preserveTrekPathZoneTrails) {
 			renderChannel(chan, chan->_lastRenderedBbox, blitTo, chan == hiliteChannel);
 		}
 		renderChannel(chan, bbox, blitTo, chan == hiliteChannel);
